        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PART VI, SECTION B, LINE 11B</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>FORM 990 WAS REVIEWED BY THE CEO AND THE SECRETARY/ TREASURER. A COPY OF THE 990 IS PROVIDED TO BOARD MEMBERS PRIOR TO SUBMISSION TO THE IRS.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PART VI, SECTION B, LINE 12C</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>A CONTRACT OR TRANSACTION IN WHICH A DIRECTOR OR OFFICER HAS FINANCIAL INTEREST, SHALL ONLY BE AUTHORIZED BY THE BOARD OF THE DIRECTORS OR THE COMMITTEE THEREOF UNDER THE FOLLOWING CONDITIONS: A) THE MATERIAL FACTS OF THE RELATIONSHIP OR INTEREST AS TO THE CONTRACT OR TRANSACTION ARE FULLY DISCLOSED TO THE BOARD OF DIRECTORS OR COMMITTEE WHO AUTHORIZES THE CONTRACT OR TRANSACTION BY THE AFFIRMATIVE VOTE OF A MAJORITY OF THE DISINTERESTED DIRECTORS AND OFFICERS B) THE CONTRACT OR TRANSACTION IS FAIR AS TO THE CORPORATION AS OF THE TIME IT IS AUTHORIZED, APPROVED OR RATIFIED BY THE BOARD OF DIRECTORS. AT A MEETING OF THE BOARD OF DIRECTORS IN WHICH THE AUTHORIZATION OF A CONTRACT OR TRANSACTION IS IN QUESTION, THE COMMON OR INTERESTED DIRECTORS MAY BE COUNTED IN DETERMINING THE PRESCENCE OF A QUORUM.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PART VI, SECTION B, LINE 15</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>APPROVED COMPENSATION PACKAGE FOR CEO WAS BASED ON COMPENSATION STUDY PREPARED BY A THIRD PARTY. IN ADDITION OTHER OFFICER'S COMPENSATION WAS BASED ON REVIEWING COMPARABLE DATA FROM SIMILAR FIRMS AND REPORTED SALARIES FOR MACHINE LEARNING ENGINEERS IN THE BAY AREA, AND AGGREGATED DATA FROM PAYFACTORS FOR POSITIONS IN OPERATIONS AND MANAGEMENT. THE ORGANIZATION ALSO CONSIDERED OFFER LETTERS RECEIVED BY INDIVIDUALS ON THE STAFF FROM OTHER ORGANIZATIONS, AS WELL AS PUBLICLY AVAILABLE NONPROFIT REPORTED SALARIES FROM SIMILAR ORGANIZATIONS SUCH AS OPENAI. THE PROCESS IS DOCUMENTED. THE ORGANIZATION CONSIDERED ALL OF THE DATA, AND THE RESPONSIBILITIES AND EXPERTISE REQUIRED OF THE VARIOUS POSITIONS TO DETERMINE DIFFERENT SALARY AMOUNTS FOR DIFFERENT POSITIONS AND LEVELS WITHIN THOSE POSITIONS. FURTHERMORE, THE ORGANIZATION HIRED A LAW FIRM TO PROVIDE AND INDEPENDENT REVIEW AND RECOMMENDATION FOR THE COMPENSATION POLICY.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
